### Parser Configuration
- `language_detection`: "auto" (auto-detect or specify: `--language python`)
- `offline_parsing": true (whether to use offline parsers, default: true)
- `cache_parsers": true (whether to cache parsed parsers, default: true)
- `parallel_parsing": true (whether to parse in parallel, default: true for multi-core)
- `max_concurrent_parses": 8 (maximum concurrent parse operations, default: 8)
- `memory_limit_mb": 2048 (memory limit for parsing in MB, default: 2048)

### AST Navigation Settings
- `navigate_to_imports": true (whether to navigate to import statements, default: true)
- `navigate_to_functions": true (whether to navigate to function definitions, default: true)
- `navigate_to_classes": true (whether to navigate to class definitions, default: true)
- `navigate_to_methods": true (whether to navigate to method definitions, default: true)
- `navigate_to_variables": true (whether to navigate to variable declarations, default: true)

## Skeleton Extraction Algorithm

### 1. Abstract Syntax Tree Parsing
```
Function: parse_ast()
Inputs:
  - file_path: path to source file
  - language: programming language (auto-detected if not specified)
  - options: {language_detection, offline_parsing, cache_parsers, parallel_parsing}
Outputs:
  - ast: Abstract Syntax Tree representation
  - parse_success: boolean indicating successful parsing
  - parse_errors: list of any parse errors encountered
  - processing_time: time taken for parsing in milliseconds
```

### 2. Skeleton Extraction
```
Function: extract_skeleton()
Inputs:
  - ast: Abstract Syntax Tree from parse_ast()
  - options: {preserve_logic, remove_redundant_imports, optimize_whitespace, language_specific_rules}
Outputs:
  - skeleton: Minimal functional skeleton preserving all executable logic
  - removed_elements: list of removed non-essential elements
  - preservation_report: report on functional equivalence (100% claimed)
  - reduction_percentage: calculated token reduction (target: 30-40%)
```

### 3. Redundant Import Removal
```
Function: remove_redundant_imports()
Inputs:
  - ast: Abstract Syntax Tree
  - options: {cross_reference_usage, language_specific_import_patterns}
Outputs:
  - cleaned_ast: AST with unused imports removed
  - removed_imports: list of imports identified as unused
  - import_analysis: detailed analysis of import usage across codebase
  - reduction_percentage: token reduction from import removal (5-10%)
```

### 4. Comment Optimization
```
Function: optimize_comments()
Inputs:
  - ast: Abstract Syntax Tree
  - options: {preserve_docs, remove_redundant, classify_types, language_specific_rules}
Outputs:
  - optimized_ast: AST with optimized comments
  - removed_comments: list of comments removed as redundant
  - preserved_comments: list of essential comments preserved
  - classification_report: report on comment types (20+ types classified)
  - reduction_percentage: token reduction from comment optimization (8-12%)
```

### 5. White-Space & Formatting Normalization
```
Function: normalize_whitespace()
Inputs:
  - ast: Abstract Syntax Tree
  - options: {aggressive, preserve_style, language_specific_rules}
Outputs:
  - normalized_ast: AST with normalized white-space and formatting
  - formatting_changes: list of formatting changes made
  - preserved_functionality: boolean verifying no functionality loss
  - reduction_percentage: token reduction from whitespace normalization (3-7%)
```

