## Common Phase 3 Issues & Resolutions

| Issue | Resolution |
|-------|------------|
| Tree-sitter not supporting language | Check `draco treesitter --list-languages`, install missing parser |
| Skeleton removes essential logic | Use `--aggressive false`, start with L1, gradually increase to L3 |
| Very slow parsing on large codebases | Use `--parallel true`, `--max-concurrent 8`, consider chunked processing |
| Reduced code fails to execute | Use `--preserve-imports true`, review `--import-threshold` setting |
| Multi-language parsing errors | Specify languages explicitly: `--languages python,javascript` |
| Import removal too aggressive | Increase `--import-threshold` (default: removes if usage < 2 references) |
| Comment optimization removes essential docs | Use `--preserve-docs true`, review classification report |

## Integration with Other Phases

### Phase 3 → Phase 1
- Skeleton extraction results feed into baseline metrics update
- Reduction percentages from Phase 3 adjust Phase 1 reduction targets
- Functional equivalence results become Phase 1 quality baseline

### Phase 3 → Phase 2
- Zero-LLM routing skips Tree-sitter processing for identified deterministic commands
- Reduction percentages combine: zero-LLM (40%) + skeleton (40%) = cumulative effect
- Deterministic commands' skeletons pre-extracted and cached

### Phase 3 → Phase 4
- Skeletons provide reduced context for BM25+ONNX RAG (smaller context = faster scoring)
- Import removal results inform BM25 keyword indexing
- Comment optimization results reduce noise in semantic similarity scoring

### Phase 3 → Phase 5
- Skeletons provide reduced input for YAML filter training (fewer tokens, faster training)
- Import/export patterns inform YAML filter rule generation
- Comment classification informs filter exclude/include patterns

### Phase 3 → Phase 9
- Skeleton sparsity informs pruning targets (40-50% sparsity from skeleton baseline)
- Reduced code provides fewer tokens for model-aware quantization
- Skeletion quality (98%+) sets quality floor for Phase 9 pruning

## Skill Execution

### Command Line
```bash
# Initialize DraCo with Phase 3 Tree-sitter
draco init --phase 3

# Parse codebase with Tree-sitter
draco treesitter --parse --input ./my-project --output ./skeleton/

# Extract skeleton with YAGNI level 3
draco skeleton --extract --aggressive false --yanagi-level 3

# Parse specific languages
draco treesitter --parse --languages python,javascript --input ./project

# View parsing statistics
draco treesitter --stats --input ./my-project

# Check supported languages
draco treesitter --list-languages
```

### Skill File Integration
This skill file is auto-loaded by DraCo at session start and integrates with:
- `.claude/skills/draco-baseline.skill` (Phase 1 - baseline for skeleton extraction priorities)
- `.claude/skills/draco-mcp-integration.skill` (Phase 2 - skip zero-LLM commands from skeleton)
- `.claude/skills/draco-hybrid-rag.skill` (Phase 4 - reduced skeleton context for RAG)
- `.claude/skills/draco-agent-hooks.skill` (Phase 10 - per-agent skeleton extraction settings)

### Dependencies
- Requires: `tree-sitter >= 0.20.0`, `tree-sitter-python >= 0.20.0`, etc. (30+ parsers)
- Requires: `draco-core >= 1.0`, `draco-nlp >= 1.0`
- Optional: `draco-mcp >= 1.0` (for zero-LLM skipping during skeleton extraction)
- Compatible with: All 50+ DraCo agent integrations

